      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The irregular pressure spikes you're seeing are likely caused by mechanical binding between the torque converter and engine due to poor exhaust back pressure rather than a faulty transmission unit. Modern Hamilton Sundstrand units generally require only the first sensor to switch on per bypass event, so if a shifter isn't fully disengaged when the transmit component shifts, it indicates a clearing issue in the shift logic. Before sending the unit apart for major testing, have the vehicle timer cleared to address the common shift neutral regulation question first.",
