      "content": "Given your pristine exhaust and specific 2-3 and 3-4 shift issues, a failed shift solenoid is the most probable culprit, likely stuck slightly or blowing past. These specific gear transitions are notoriously difficult for modern Hamilton Sundstrand transmissions, and you should immediately inspect the corresponding 18N or 20N solenoid for debris and a quality seal check. If the solenoids are clean and seized, the next logical step is a valve body rebuild to rule out internal hydraulic pressure lockouts before considering the transmission itself.",
