      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the solenoids appear fresh and free-moving, the erratic pressure spikes are likely caused by a poor seal on a specific valve body pivot pin or worn laterals on the tone ring. In these older F-150 transmissions, minor debris can create variable clearance that manifests as pressure spikes only under heavy load without obvious external symptoms. Replacing the correct pivot pin seals first is usually the most cost-effective way to eliminate these hydraulic irregularities before moving to more invasive internal testing.",
